WEBVTT

00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:12.930
Miguel Jump sequence complete.

00:00:12.930 --> 00:00:14.730
We're out in normal space.

00:00:14.730 --> 00:00:17.320
Deploying spatial mesh with
Vega as the base coordinate.

00:00:17.320 --> 00:00:19.560
Warp coordinates within expected range.

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:24.720
Clair, get the advance Orichalt
torpedo ready for another launch.

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:27.740
Girlie, where's the satellite pursuing that's us?

00:00:27.740 --> 00:00:32.920
Based on visual observation data, it doesn't
appear to have followed us through the warp.

00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:36.330
Distance from our ship is over 100 AU.

00:00:36.330 --> 00:00:37.710
It's not moving?

00:00:37.710 --> 00:00:40.240
Maybe it gave up?

00:02:32.930 --> 00:02:34.010
Papa!

00:02:34.010 --> 00:02:36.620
It looks like that satellite
is trying to find our location!

00:02:36.620 --> 00:02:40.350
What a pain in the ass we've attracted!

00:02:40.350 --> 00:02:41.770
What now?

00:02:41.770 --> 00:02:43.770
We can't work or accept requests like that.

00:02:43.770 --> 00:02:44.910
Ido.

00:02:44.910 --> 00:02:50.680
That satellite leaving its planet and coming after
us has to be because of her, don't you think?

00:02:50.680 --> 00:02:51.530
Yeah.

00:02:51.530 --> 00:02:54.730
At the very least, there has
to be some relation.

00:02:54.730 --> 00:02:55.890
Mr. Ido.

00:02:56.290 --> 00:03:03.650
When we touched the Orichalt vein back there,
a bunch of images flowed into our brain units, right?

00:03:03.650 --> 00:03:08.550
I think those were someone's memory information
that transferred through Orichalt somehow.

00:03:08.840 --> 00:03:15.050
Maybe if we find out whose memories those were we'll
have a better picture of the whole chain of events?

00:03:15.050 --> 00:03:16.990
Someone's memories transferring?

00:03:16.990 --> 00:03:17.930
From where?

00:03:17.930 --> 00:03:18.940
Transfer?

00:03:18.940 --> 00:03:19.940
What memories?

00:03:19.940 --> 00:03:21.260
What are you talking about, Ido?

00:03:21.260 --> 00:03:22.920
It's nothing important.

00:03:22.920 --> 00:03:27.280
Just some influence on the brain units
from contact with Orichalt ore.

00:03:27.280 --> 00:03:30.320
But we both saw the same images!

00:03:30.320 --> 00:03:33.960
There's got to be some connection
between those images and her appearing!

00:03:33.960 --> 00:03:35.700
Her appearing?

00:03:36.320 --> 00:03:39.040
I don't think I'm your enemy anymore.

00:03:39.040 --> 00:03:40.910
If you have any secrets, I want to know.

00:03:40.910 --> 00:03:42.540
Well, you see...

00:03:42.540 --> 00:03:43.090
Rick!

00:03:43.090 --> 00:03:44.370
Yes!

00:03:44.370 --> 00:03:47.840
Coincidence or not,
you're involved in this incident now.

00:03:47.840 --> 00:03:49.750
You have a right to know.

00:03:49.750 --> 00:03:50.720
Is that alright?

00:03:50.720 --> 00:03:52.090
Do what you want.

00:03:52.400 --> 00:03:54.760
I'll say this in advance, though.

00:03:54.760 --> 00:03:56.640
Throw away your common sense.

00:04:13.030 --> 00:04:15.040
What is that?

00:04:15.040 --> 00:04:18.780
Well, when we were checking the
Orichalt extracted from that new planet-

00:04:19.480 --> 00:04:21.220
That's what happened!

00:04:21.220 --> 00:04:24.540
By the way, this video has not been
tampered with in any way.

00:04:24.540 --> 00:04:26.830
Why didn't you inform the military about this?

00:04:27.130 --> 00:04:29.750
They demanded Orichalt.

00:04:29.750 --> 00:04:32.210
Nobody said anything about the
brat that was inside it.

00:04:33.510 --> 00:04:35.760
Did you inspect her body?

00:04:35.760 --> 00:04:37.120
Obviously.

00:04:37.120 --> 00:04:40.470
It would be bad if some unknown virus
were to spread through the ship.

00:04:41.240 --> 00:04:43.650
Skeleton, internal organs, blood.

00:04:43.650 --> 00:04:47.470
Apart from there being trace amounts
of silicon in her extra cellular matrix,

00:04:47.470 --> 00:04:49.540
she's pretty much identical to a human.

00:04:49.540 --> 00:04:54.250
Based on Hayflick limit measurement, she appears
to be around 4 years old in human age.

00:04:54.250 --> 00:04:59.070
Apart from her being unable to speak, she's
basically a normal healthy 4-year old girl.

00:04:59.070 --> 00:05:04.960
We assume she was inside the Orichalt because
of getting involved in a spatial warp somehow,

00:05:04.960 --> 00:05:08.000
but that doesn't explain how
she was able to stay alive...

00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:10.820
She's the one the satellite's after.

00:05:10.820 --> 00:05:12.400
That's what you're thinking, right?

00:05:12.400 --> 00:05:14.770
We're not certain, but the possibility is high.

00:05:14.770 --> 00:05:17.470
There aren't any other reasons we can think of.

00:05:17.470 --> 00:05:19.130
Just by means of elimination.

00:05:19.130 --> 00:05:22.430
While that's not something I can readily accept,

00:05:22.430 --> 00:05:25.310
if it's the truth, there's a way to deal with this.

00:05:25.310 --> 00:05:29.440
We put this girl into a capsule, direct
it at the satellite and fire away.

00:05:29.440 --> 00:05:31.560
That way it's not going to chase
us and we're done.

00:05:31.560 --> 00:05:32.560
What?

00:05:32.560 --> 00:05:33.760
That's awful!

00:05:33.760 --> 00:05:35.230
That's a pretty simple way of thinking.

00:05:35.570 --> 00:05:36.570
What?!

00:05:36.570 --> 00:05:40.500
The satellite is one thing,
but I'm concerned about the military.

00:05:40.500 --> 00:05:45.450
What if the people who sent in the orders
to catch our ship were after Ore?

00:05:45.450 --> 00:05:46.450
Ore?

00:05:46.450 --> 00:05:47.660
Codename.

00:05:47.660 --> 00:05:48.500
Hers.

00:05:48.500 --> 00:05:50.500
You even gave her a name?

00:05:50.760 --> 00:05:52.900
And where's the problem in that?

00:05:52.900 --> 00:05:55.980
The problem is if the military's
goal really was Ore.

00:05:55.980 --> 00:06:01.080
If you don't know, lieutenant, it might be some
dangerous info only the higher-ups have access to.

00:06:01.080 --> 00:06:04.130
We can't let our trump card go so easily.

00:06:04.130 --> 00:06:05.570
Trump card?

00:06:05.570 --> 00:06:07.850
We can use her in negotiations.

00:06:07.850 --> 00:06:08.770
Captain!

00:06:08.770 --> 00:06:10.640
She's alive!

00:06:10.640 --> 00:06:12.340
She's young and fragile!

00:06:12.340 --> 00:06:15.860
Aren't we supposed to protect her from harm?

00:06:15.860 --> 00:06:18.160
Using her in negotiatons-

00:06:18.160 --> 00:06:19.660
Girlie.

00:06:19.660 --> 00:06:22.830
I'm no god, and I'm not almighty.

00:06:22.830 --> 00:06:25.320
I'm just a military man who got fired.

00:06:25.320 --> 00:06:26.160
But you see,

00:06:26.160 --> 00:06:31.210
I don't want to lose my ship,
body or crew members.

00:06:31.210 --> 00:06:34.210
And to protect those, I'll do anything.

00:06:34.210 --> 00:06:35.210
You hear me?!

00:06:35.210 --> 00:06:36.340
Anything!

00:06:45.010 --> 00:06:47.010
You didn't have to be so hard on her.

00:06:47.160 --> 00:06:48.220
Leave her alone.

00:06:48.220 --> 00:06:51.560
We don't need anything but cold,
hard reason on this ship.

00:06:51.560 --> 00:06:55.000
So, Pops, what are we going to do in the end?

00:06:55.000 --> 00:06:56.390
It's obvious, isn't it?

00:06:56.390 --> 00:07:02.060
Go towards the Miguel Net territory through the shortest
route while staying wary of the military and the satellite.

00:07:02.060 --> 00:07:04.490
Maintaining the status quo, then.

00:07:04.490 --> 00:07:07.410
So the boring days are gonna continue, then?

00:07:11.020 --> 00:07:12.580
Listen here, girlie.

00:07:12.880 --> 00:07:18.260
Say as many pretty words as you'd like, they're
pointless if you don't have a proper plan.

00:07:18.260 --> 00:07:20.750
Can't you even understand that, you brat?

00:07:21.760 --> 00:07:23.590
That was bad...

00:07:23.590 --> 00:07:26.090
I couldn't think of a single word in response...

00:07:26.760 --> 00:07:29.520
I really haven't done anything...

00:07:41.030 --> 00:07:41.870
Here you go.

00:07:46.240 --> 00:07:48.610
Guess there's no time to be moping around.

00:07:49.450 --> 00:07:51.830
I have to do what I have to do.

00:07:51.830 --> 00:07:53.840
And what I can do right now is...

00:07:56.500 --> 00:07:58.560
For starters, the observation data-

00:07:59.090 --> 00:08:00.760
Extravehicular activity?

00:08:00.760 --> 00:08:01.680
Who is it?

00:08:20.680 --> 00:08:21.690
What do you want?

00:08:24.780 --> 00:08:26.060
I've got a question.

00:08:28.080 --> 00:08:30.160
Why don't you have memories?

00:08:31.330 --> 00:08:33.080
No memories?

00:08:33.400 --> 00:08:35.510
Trouble during a Mind Trance?

00:08:35.510 --> 00:08:38.500
Or did your brain unit take damage?

00:08:38.790 --> 00:08:42.140
I have no memories,
how am I supposed to talk about my past?

00:08:42.140 --> 00:08:45.400
In that case, when did you regain consciousness?

00:08:45.400 --> 00:08:47.800
7 years ago, on an exile ship.

00:08:48.080 --> 00:08:49.420
An exile ship?

00:08:49.420 --> 00:08:51.840
They only send A-class criminals on those.

00:08:52.090 --> 00:08:53.170
Looks like it.

00:08:53.170 --> 00:08:54.320
For what crime?

00:08:54.320 --> 00:08:56.350
I keep telling you, I don't remember.

00:08:57.810 --> 00:09:02.150
When I awakened, I was already
aboard the exile ship.

00:09:02.570 --> 00:09:07.550
I had feelings and knowledge, it was just
my memories that were entirely lacking

00:09:07.860 --> 00:09:13.860
Not even able to remember my own name,
with the ID proving my existence gone too.

00:09:14.170 --> 00:09:16.500
Going off the machine production time,

00:09:16.500 --> 00:09:21.810
I was probably imprisoned as an I-machine
for more than 20 years.

00:09:23.560 --> 00:09:25.650
After I regained consciousness,

00:09:25.650 --> 00:09:28.930
continued being there, unable to meet anyone.

00:09:29.590 --> 00:09:31.530
What am I?

00:09:31.530 --> 00:09:33.300
What crime did I commit?

00:09:33.300 --> 00:09:35.100
Why don't I have a body?

00:09:35.100 --> 00:09:37.060
How long is my sentence?

00:09:37.060 --> 00:09:39.600
I had endless time to think.

00:09:39.600 --> 00:09:43.160
Or rather, there was nothing I could do but think.

00:09:43.160 --> 00:09:45.620
There was no answer.

00:09:46.040 --> 00:09:49.920
But then those hellish days suddenly ended.

00:09:50.490 --> 00:09:58.620
My consciousness Mind Tranced once again and
transferred to this machine, stranded in space.

00:09:59.110 --> 00:10:03.890
I don't know how, but I do know
I escaped the exile ship.

00:10:04.630 --> 00:10:07.040
My course was clear from that point onwards.

00:10:07.040 --> 00:10:13.690
Without an ID, I'd only be accepted in the
criminal world or in life-risking jobs.

00:10:13.690 --> 00:10:16.770
And in the end, I ended up drifting here.

00:10:16.770 --> 00:10:19.180
You didn't try to find out about your past?

00:10:19.180 --> 00:10:21.220
Of course I did.

00:10:21.450 --> 00:10:25.800
But there weren't records of anyone
getting captured in an I-machine.

00:10:25.800 --> 00:10:29.400
And without memories,
I had no other leads to go off.

00:10:29.400 --> 00:10:33.890
So now you're living to find out
who you were before?

00:10:33.890 --> 00:10:35.010
I don't know about that.

00:10:35.530 --> 00:10:38.000
What's the point in learning the past now?

00:10:38.000 --> 00:10:43.880
This body, this mind and the time I've spent
living with those are what makes me up now.

00:10:43.880 --> 00:10:46.090
Ido the Excavator.

00:10:46.090 --> 00:10:48.500
That's my entire being now.

00:10:48.500 --> 00:10:52.860
I didn't expect you to answer so in-detail.

00:10:52.860 --> 00:10:56.050
There were other people who
wanted to hear this, you see.

00:11:00.600 --> 00:11:02.470
I didn't mean to...

00:11:03.610 --> 00:11:06.480
Wait, could those images...

00:11:09.920 --> 00:11:12.040
Stop it! Don't look at me...

00:11:12.040 --> 00:11:13.340
Humanity is already...

00:11:13.340 --> 00:11:14.610
Are you saying it's pointless?!

00:11:14.610 --> 00:11:16.260
I'm sorry! Right now I...

00:11:16.260 --> 00:11:18.970
Your sin...!

00:11:38.410 --> 00:11:42.260
The EM wave observation devices
located a specific spectrum.

00:11:42.260 --> 00:11:44.200
A specific spectrum?

00:11:45.060 --> 00:11:46.250
What is it?

00:11:46.250 --> 00:11:47.860
If you've got an opinion, go on.

00:11:48.820 --> 00:11:50.020
Okay.

00:11:50.320 --> 00:11:52.680
Ms. Claire, is it space dust?

00:11:52.680 --> 00:11:53.610
Yeah.

00:11:53.610 --> 00:11:56.680
But there wasn't anything
when I checked an hour ago.

00:11:56.680 --> 00:11:58.080
What's up with this?

00:11:58.080 --> 00:12:00.040
Wasn't this supposed to be a safe route?

00:12:00.040 --> 00:12:03.680
Well there's barely any info on celestial
bodies outside the Miguel Net.

00:12:03.680 --> 00:12:08.380
Their thin and cold so they emit little radiation,
we probably couldn't detect them because of that.

00:12:09.030 --> 00:12:14.900
Normally we'd evade it, but I'd rather not change
the orbit to get away from that satellite...

00:12:14.900 --> 00:12:19.050
Find high-density cores and calculate
the risk of going through the cloud.

00:12:20.100 --> 00:12:21.520
Okay.

00:12:21.520 --> 00:12:24.050
Third hangar here, Ido just came back.

00:12:24.050 --> 00:12:24.640
Got it.

00:12:24.640 --> 00:12:26.720
Oh hey, Amanza's with you too?

00:12:26.720 --> 00:12:27.950
Now that's shifty.

00:12:27.950 --> 00:12:29.500
What were you two doing there?

00:12:29.500 --> 00:12:30.400
Having a date.

00:12:30.400 --> 00:12:32.130
A date, eh.

00:12:32.130 --> 00:12:33.200
Wait, what?!

00:12:33.200 --> 00:12:33.940
Seriously?

00:12:33.940 --> 00:12:35.440
Hey! Hey! Hey!

00:12:35.440 --> 00:12:37.280
How come I didn't know?

00:12:37.280 --> 00:12:39.460
Why didn't you tell me?

00:12:39.460 --> 00:12:41.750
Are the analysis results ready yet?

00:12:41.750 --> 00:12:42.960
Oh, yes.

00:12:42.960 --> 00:12:48.050
More than 90% of it is hydrogen,
the rest is silicon and carbon.

00:12:48.050 --> 00:12:49.970
I'm detecting iron too.

00:12:49.970 --> 00:12:54.420
The density is thin, but we shouldn't
underestimate the kinetic energy if we collide.

00:12:54.420 --> 00:12:56.020
I'd refrain from a Miguel Jump-

00:12:56.020 --> 00:12:58.860
Can we go through? Or not?

00:12:59.890 --> 00:13:07.490
If we deploy the bumpers to block meteoroids and the
magnetic field to repel space dust, we probably can.

00:13:07.490 --> 00:13:09.310
You should've said that right away!

00:13:09.310 --> 00:13:11.980
You were the one who asked me
yo calculate risks, captain!

00:13:15.030 --> 00:13:16.980
We're going through the cloud.

00:13:16.980 --> 00:13:18.890
Everyone, standby in the hangars!

00:13:18.890 --> 00:13:19.990
Got it!

00:13:30.380 --> 00:13:33.840
Deployment of bumpers towards
the ship's course complete!

00:13:33.840 --> 00:13:36.720
Sealing all bulkheads inside the ship!

00:13:37.060 --> 00:13:41.450
Release all of the dust caught
in the bumpers as propellant.

00:13:41.450 --> 00:13:44.310
Even if there are useful resources
in them, ignore them!

00:13:51.400 --> 00:13:54.540
Stulti has entered the cloud.

00:13:55.690 --> 00:13:57.900
Bumpers and magnetic field, all green.

00:14:01.660 --> 00:14:04.540
Ore, stay there for a while, okay?

00:14:04.540 --> 00:14:06.370
I'll play with you later.

00:14:07.690 --> 00:14:11.540
Ms. Amanza, please look after her.

00:14:11.540 --> 00:14:13.040
Why me?

00:14:13.040 --> 00:14:16.740
Sorry, there isn't anyone else to ask.

00:14:18.440 --> 00:14:20.930
Is that the influence of the forced magnetic field?

00:14:21.890 --> 00:14:22.760
Papa!

00:14:22.760 --> 00:14:24.470
Code yellow on the monitoring system!

00:14:24.470 --> 00:14:25.900
In the 15th block!

00:14:26.890 --> 00:14:30.270
The hull mass and gravity numbers are changing!

00:14:30.270 --> 00:14:31.530
Why?

00:14:31.530 --> 00:14:32.910
Bring up the visual data!

00:14:34.560 --> 00:14:35.810
The hell is this?

00:14:35.810 --> 00:14:38.120
Fog? No, sand?

00:14:38.120 --> 00:14:41.890
Could the space dust have entered the ship?

00:14:41.890 --> 00:14:43.710
Girlie, analyze it!

00:14:43.710 --> 00:14:46.090
You don't have to tell me, I'm doing it.

00:14:49.520 --> 00:14:51.890
It's the same as that satellite!

00:14:51.890 --> 00:14:53.690
It's ahead of us?

00:14:53.690 --> 00:14:55.580
Did a part of the satellite jump?

00:14:55.580 --> 00:14:56.740
No way!

00:14:56.740 --> 00:14:59.330
Without Orichalt? How did it jump?

00:14:59.330 --> 00:15:05.550
I assume there were trace amounts of Orichalt
in the space dust that we couldn't detect.

00:15:05.550 --> 00:15:08.390
To be able to jump with just trace amounts...

00:15:08.390 --> 00:15:12.520
Did it consciously pulverize itself
to reduce the mass of each part?

00:15:12.520 --> 00:15:13.890
No way.

00:15:13.890 --> 00:15:17.220
You telling me that satellite turned
to sand and jumped over here?

00:15:17.220 --> 00:15:23.940
If my guess is right, then the mass that can jump
with just trace amounts of Orichalt isn't that big.

00:15:23.940 --> 00:15:28.490
But as the time passes, more and
more of it will warp here.

00:15:28.490 --> 00:15:31.890
Using it as a propellant backfired, huh...

00:15:31.890 --> 00:15:33.790
Clair, close the bumpers.

00:15:34.290 --> 00:15:37.380
Let's rely on just the magnetic
field to handle the collisions.

00:15:37.380 --> 00:15:39.370
Don't let any more of it into the ship.

00:15:39.370 --> 00:15:39.880
Got it!

00:15:40.090 --> 00:15:42.760
Girlie, how much until we're out of here?

00:15:42.760 --> 00:15:45.800
If we change our route,
the shortest it will take is 23 minutes.

00:15:45.800 --> 00:15:47.260
Where's the sand heading?

00:15:47.260 --> 00:15:48.890
Straight towards the gravity-enabled quarters!

00:15:48.890 --> 00:15:50.860
It really is after that brat then.

00:15:50.860 --> 00:15:52.480
Isn't that bad?

00:15:52.480 --> 00:15:55.520
The bulkheads are sealed,
that sand shouldn't get through.

00:15:57.630 --> 00:15:58.690
Hey! It's moving!

00:15:58.690 --> 00:16:00.770
There are no changes to the hull mass!

00:16:01.110 --> 00:16:05.580
From sand to elementary particle level...
It's using quantum tunneling to pass.

00:16:06.140 --> 00:16:07.480
It's out!

00:16:07.480 --> 00:16:08.950
At this rate, that girl will-

00:16:08.950 --> 00:16:13.320
Lieutenant Amanza! Can you hear me?
Lieutenant! Shit! The comms are...

00:16:15.040 --> 00:16:16.130
Where are you going?

00:16:16.130 --> 00:16:17.540
To protect that girl!

00:16:17.540 --> 00:16:18.800
Is that wrong?

00:16:18.800 --> 00:16:22.510
I can get to their room before the sand if I go now!

00:16:22.510 --> 00:16:24.100
That's crazy, Maya!

00:16:24.100 --> 00:16:24.920
Go!

00:16:25.390 --> 00:16:26.650
Mr. Ido?

00:16:26.650 --> 00:16:29.460
Head towards the escape shuttle
in the 24th block.

00:16:29.460 --> 00:16:30.890
We'll make the rest work out somehow.

00:16:30.890 --> 00:16:32.400
I'm counting on you!

00:16:32.820 --> 00:16:34.710
Somehow? What are we supposed to do?

00:16:34.710 --> 00:16:38.160
We can't get into the human-sized blocks!

00:16:38.160 --> 00:16:39.350
There's a way.

00:16:39.910 --> 00:16:41.190
Help me out.

00:16:47.990 --> 00:16:49.150
The time?

00:16:50.290 --> 00:16:51.270
It's alright.

00:16:53.120 --> 00:16:55.080
We're going to the 24th block!

00:16:55.080 --> 00:16:56.460
Follow me!

00:16:57.460 --> 00:16:58.210
What is it-

00:16:58.210 --> 00:16:59.650
Hurry up!

00:17:01.660 --> 00:17:05.510
What do you mean, a part of the
satellite has entered the ship?

00:17:05.510 --> 00:17:06.900
I'm saying,-

00:17:10.400 --> 00:17:11.520
That's-

00:17:11.720 --> 00:17:13.350
It's faster than predicted!

00:17:13.350 --> 00:17:14.560
Here!

00:17:16.320 --> 00:17:18.520
Maya and the rest are leaving
the gravity-enabled block.

00:17:18.730 --> 00:17:19.920
Hey! Ido!

00:17:19.920 --> 00:17:20.850
Just a bit more!

00:17:22.440 --> 00:17:23.900
Let's hurry!

00:17:25.340 --> 00:17:26.620
The escape shuttle?

00:17:26.620 --> 00:17:27.700
You want to get outside?

00:17:27.700 --> 00:17:28.990
Mr. Ido said to.

00:17:28.990 --> 00:17:29.950
He did?

00:17:37.750 --> 00:17:40.090
It formed into a solid object?

00:17:40.090 --> 00:17:41.290
It can do even that?

00:17:41.290 --> 00:17:43.560
If it's after this girl, let's leave her here.

00:17:43.560 --> 00:17:44.720
We can't do that!

00:17:44.720 --> 00:17:46.000
There aren't any other choices!

00:17:46.000 --> 00:17:47.220
There are!

00:17:47.220 --> 00:17:53.840
Uh, well, strictly speaking, for me there aren't
any, but he said it'd work out somehow...

00:17:53.840 --> 00:17:54.720
It's coming!

00:17:58.780 --> 00:17:59.850
Run!

00:18:01.340 --> 00:18:02.440
That voice!

00:18:02.720 --> 00:18:03.940
Mr. Ido?

00:18:03.940 --> 00:18:07.620
Did you Trance into the automatic
maintenance machines?

00:18:07.620 --> 00:18:10.280
We're only 1/5th connected with them, though.

00:18:10.280 --> 00:18:14.620
Based on the change in hull mass,
only this part entered the ship.

00:18:14.620 --> 00:18:15.570
Let's stop it!

00:18:15.570 --> 00:18:16.530
Got it!

00:18:18.530 --> 00:18:19.780
Did it!

00:18:22.570 --> 00:18:24.290
It can run away like that?

00:18:24.290 --> 00:18:26.040
That's just cheating!

00:18:31.680 --> 00:18:33.530
Next plan, Grayman!

00:18:34.110 --> 00:18:34.980
Leave it to me!

00:18:34.980 --> 00:18:37.220
Maya and the rest, grab onto something!

00:18:37.220 --> 00:18:38.620
We're releasing the shuttle!

00:18:39.140 --> 00:18:40.520
Suddenly like that!

00:18:41.100 --> 00:18:43.750
Close your eyes!
Breathe all the air out!

00:18:51.200 --> 00:18:52.990
Hold tight, okay!

00:19:07.390 --> 00:19:08.260
Okay!

00:19:08.260 --> 00:19:09.760
Collision course!

00:19:09.760 --> 00:19:10.760
Mind Out!

00:19:31.110 --> 00:19:32.440
No way!

00:19:32.440 --> 00:19:37.200
No!

00:19:37.200 --> 00:19:39.610
No...

00:19:47.610 --> 00:19:49.030
Too late...

00:19:53.860 --> 00:19:56.570
I had to protect her, but...

00:19:58.050 --> 00:20:00.360
I couldn't do anything...

00:20:10.930 --> 00:20:11.780
She's alive?

00:20:13.290 --> 00:20:14.570
Alive?

00:20:14.570 --> 00:20:15.560
How?

00:20:16.520 --> 00:20:19.060
What is going on?

00:20:25.850 --> 00:20:27.140
Come here, Alice.

00:20:29.430 --> 00:20:30.340
Alice.

00:20:34.580 --> 00:20:37.460
Was that my voice?

00:20:37.810 --> 00:20:39.400
From back when I had a body?

00:20:40.860 --> 00:20:43.570
It called you... Alice.

00:20:44.290 --> 00:20:45.680
It called you Alice.

00:20:54.890 --> 00:20:55.930
What's with him?

00:20:58.110 --> 00:21:03.240
To find something I've given up on
and tried forgetting in a place like this...

00:21:03.900 --> 00:21:05.040
That's right.

00:21:06.310 --> 00:21:07.300
You are...

00:21:08.210 --> 00:21:09.610
My past!

00:22:44.990 --> 00:22:48.820
Well, you see, I don't want you
to go overboard.

00:22:48.820 --> 00:22:51.190
You're an important employee too, girlie.

00:22:51.600 --> 00:22:53.520
I'm sorry, Maya.

00:22:53.520 --> 00:22:56.400
My papa is pretty rough with words.

00:22:56.400 --> 00:22:58.190
Forgive him, alright?

00:22:58.280 --> 00:22:59.840
Forgive him?

00:22:59.840 --> 00:23:02.780
I thought I was the one hated here...

00:23:02.780 --> 00:23:04.120
The other way around!

00:23:04.120 --> 00:23:07.250
Papa was really worried that you hated him.

00:23:08.500 --> 00:23:09.500
That's how it is!

00:23:09.500 --> 00:23:12.780
Well, uh, let's get along!

00:23:12.780 --> 00:23:15.100
As fellow miners in the same space!

00:23:15.100 --> 00:23:16.350
Sure!

00:23:16.350 --> 00:23:18.560
Wait, I'm still a student!

00:23:20.730 --> 00:23:22.200
Isn't that fine?

00:23:22.200 --> 00:23:23.500
No it's not!

00:23:25.800 --> 00:23:26.970
Alice.

00:23:26.970 --> 00:23:30.890
If there's a meaning in that name,
what will that pull of the trigger call?

00:23:30.890 --> 00:23:32.810
What will it lead to?

00:23:32.810 --> 00:23:36.650
When the messenger who calls himself
Observer opens the gates of hell,

00:23:36.650 --> 00:23:39.490
the thirst lying in the dark begins to move.
